WEBVTT

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.670
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.000
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:08.730
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<b>Kinou made no ruuru kyou wa tada no ruuzu</b>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:20.470
<i>Yesterday’s rules are simply loose today</i>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<b>Kowashite dantotsu gooru</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:24.520
<i>The best goal is to break them</i>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<b>hashiri tudukete nai to</b>

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>If I don’t keep running</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<b>hokani imi wa nai to</b>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.940
<i>There’s no other meaning</i>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<b>Panku na tetsukaku nanda</b>

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>It’s a punk philosophy</i>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<b>Baiorizumu wa tsuubai rizumu de</b>

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:39.330
<i>Biorhythm is a two-time rhythm</i>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<b>Fuukei wa shunkan ni musuu no sen</b>

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:43.370
<i>The scenery instantly becomes countless lines</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<b>Ore wo torimaku kaze</b>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:46.330
<i>The wind envelops me</i>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<b>Inside Outside semete</b>

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.050
<i>Inside Outside attack</i>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<b>Issai gassai nuite</b>

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.420
<i>Surpass everything altogether</i>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.430
<b>Dare hitori monani hitotsu mo</b>

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:58.140
<i>I won’t let no one and nothing go forward</i>

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.140
<b>Mae wo ikasetaku wa nai</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<b>Inside Outside GO! SONIC!!</b>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:00.470
<i>Inside Outside, Go! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<b>Issai gassai Yes! SONIC!!</b>

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.850
<i>Everything altogether Yes! Sonic!!</i>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<b>Abunai yo to Have A Nice wa niteru</b>

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.020
<i>“Watch out” and “Have a nice” are similar</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<b>Soudochira mo kamihitoe na no sa</b>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.670
<i>That’s right – both are by the skin of your teeth</i>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<b>Taikutsu nugisuteteima sugu kakedase</b>

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.160
<i>Throw boredom away and start running right now</i>

00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.290
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:24.750
<b>S, O, N, I, C, GO!</b>

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.460
<b>GO, GO, GO, GO, LET'S GO!!</b>

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.000
Are you all right?

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.130
Yeah, thank you!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.510
You can talk?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.890
Naturally, why not?

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.980
Wow, you're really talking.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.480
I... I'm Chris!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.030
And, you are?

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.990
What's your name?!

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.240
I'm Sonic.

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.030
Sonic the Hedgehog!

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.140
Episode 2

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:28.140
Infiltrate! Area 99

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:36.800
I'm sorry. Filming has been delayed because of the constant rainy weather.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:43.180
So I don't think I can return home till next week. But as a token of my apology...

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:47.270
I'll send you your presents soon by air.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.060
Okay.

00:02:48.730 --> 00:02:51.020
I got you your favorite, cotton candy, too.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.440
Thank you!

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.820
You know what mom?

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.900
Actually there's something I have to apologize to you about.

00:02:59.530 --> 00:03:00.700
What is it?

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:03.160
It's about my promise with you...

00:03:03.910 --> 00:03:09.710
About not going outside after midnight and staying away from the adult pool.

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.000
Did you swim at that time of night?

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.040
No, it's not that.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.920
I helped a drowning cat.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.840
I see. It's all right. I'm not angry at you.

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.600
You're so kind Chris. Goodbye.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.320
Was that cat supposed to be me?

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.820
Yeah. Are you angry at me?

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:44.530
You see, she wouldn't understand if I said I saved a hedgehog.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:46.200
What do you mean?

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.990
Because hedgehogs are much smaller.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.580
Maybe this big at most?

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:56.170
You're special.

00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:59.130
You're larger than normal and besides, you can talk too.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.680
Where and when did you learn to speak?

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:05.970
I wonder...

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:09.850
I don't remember something so long ago.

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.020
Really?

00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:15.190
Oh... Hello.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.900
Oh, dad...

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:25.610
Hi, Chris. Mom told me that a cat entered our pool last night?

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.080
I'm sorry, Chris!

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.040
That security's not good enough if a cat can get in so easily.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.580
Don't be. No problem. I'm just fine.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.790
I shooed it away in no time.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:42.300
It panicked and hurried off when I glared at it.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:44.760
I see.

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:49.810
Besides grandpa, Ella and Mr. Tanaka are all here with me at home.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.180
But more importantly, you're busy. Aren't you?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.940
Yeah very.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:57.230
I'm really fine, okay?

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.440
Oh okay. I'm hanging up then.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:05.030
I love you, Chris.

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:06.990
Me too, dad.

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:08.240
Bye.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:18.000
Oh by the way, what about breakfast?

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.420
What do you eat?

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:24.470
What do hedgehogs here eat?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.800
I checked it out on the Internet and this is what I found.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.770
Yuk! What is this?!

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.060
Cat food.

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.520
No way! Give me a break!

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:45.490
Well there seems to be food for hedgehogs too, but it says that cat food will do fine.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.410
You could also eat dried crickets...

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.830
Where are you going?!

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:56.910
I unfortunately happen to be a gourmet.

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:00.460
No, you shouldn't go outside!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:02.800
See you!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.260
Wait! Wait, Sonic!

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:15.100
It is so fast that it is difficult to understand just by looking at the footage.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.770
But we have some eyewitness reports.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.400
It is about this big and blue. It looks to be a hedgehog.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:25.230
It went right by me at tremendous speed.

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:28.280
No exaggeration. I'm sure he was going at mach speed.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:34.830
As to the question of whether this is a UMA - Unidentified Mutant Animal...

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:37.000
the answer is no.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:43.130
Even the cheetah, who is said to be the fastest animal around, cannot outrun a car.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:46.450
There could never be an animal who can run that fast.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:50.220
It would be more reasonable to consider it more a machine than an animal.

00:06:46.460 --> 00:06:47.300
<i>Is it good?</i>

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:55.220
It's okay, I guess.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.060
Did you hear about it, Chris!

00:06:58.230 --> 00:07:01.980
A mysterious machine that beat the S Team appeared.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:11.570
Hey, just what do you think you're doing, Chris?!

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:19.000
Blue... looks to be a hedgehog…

00:07:22.210 --> 00:07:23.420
Was it him?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:24.460
No, well, uh...

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.800
I wonder how he's made?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.800
Stop!

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:34.890
Don't run away!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:42.440
Grandpa... he... Sonic is not a machine.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.150
Please stay away.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:50.690
I'm scared.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.780
Chao!

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:56.780
Please stay away.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.870
Cream and Cheese!

00:07:58.950 --> 00:07:59.830
Do you know them?

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.620
So I'm not the only one who came to this weird world.

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.210
Okay, hang on!

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.130
Do you know where to go?!

00:08:26.980 --> 00:08:32.610
Yeah, you're a great help. Thanks. Let's get together for a meal one day soon.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:38.830
They seem to have been transported from the police to Area 99.

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:41.500
Area 99?

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:46.880
That's a military research facility!

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:48.710
Military?

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:54.470
Yeah, the National Defense Force. They have war tanks, fighter planes and weapons of war.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.970
Something like Eggman!

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.930
They've been brought to military facilities to be checked out, I see.

00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:09.570
Maybe they think you guys are some sort of aliens or biological weapons that had been developed in another country.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.740
What is in fact the truth? Huh?

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:14.240
I have no idea.

00:09:14.570 --> 00:09:18.280
So now that I know where they are, I guess I'll excuse myself.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.540
But if you go in like that, they'll catch you too.

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:23.660
I'm not such a klutz.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.710
Just what do you think you're doing?!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.540
I didn't do it!

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:30.790
I did!

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.800
This is quite interesting. I'm getting pretty excited.

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:37.630
Not you too, grandpa.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.010
You come along too.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:45.640
You're always saying that you don't want to be a bore like your dad, right?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:50.150
Agh, that's supposed to be a secret. Don't tell dad I said that.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:51.270
I know!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.530
I can't be wasting my time riding something like this.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.280
Now now.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:03.490
This is it, right?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:04.830
Right.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:07.540
Put it on.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:08.670
What is it?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:15.590
An infrared scope. I'm sure that Area 99 is full of infrared sensor traps.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:18.590
But, if you wear that, you can detect the traps.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.430
Thank you. I'm going on ahead.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:33.400
He is way faster than what I thought. Okay, then!

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:24.990
ID number F219563, match verified.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:40.720
Please let us out of here!

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:48.270
What is this place? What do plan to do with us?

00:11:57.480 --> 00:11:58.780
Do you read me, Sonic?

00:11:58.820 --> 00:11:59.190
Yeah.

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:04.070
When you get inside, go through the air vent.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.740
That should be a blind spot for security, says grandpa.

00:12:06.870 --> 00:12:07.660
All right.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:11.460
But do you know where they're being held captive?

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.660
Of course I know.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:18.380
If you keep going in suspicious looking directions, I'm sure it'll take you to your destination.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.420
Oh no. Talk about irresponsible.

00:12:21.220 --> 00:12:22.720
Oh well, I'll work it out somehow.

00:12:30.220 --> 00:12:32.980
Intruder. Verifying...

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.660
I'm inside the air vent.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:47.120
Roger.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:55.750
This sure is deep. So...

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.380
Some blind spot this is...

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:01.550
What did you just say?

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:02.880
Nothing.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:10.970
I can handle that movement hands down.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.280
Piece of cake.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:31.620
Okay, now!

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.760
Continuing verification process...

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:51.350
Continuing verification process...

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.450
I wonder if he's okay.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:38.310
This is scary.

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:49.320
This place sure looks suspicious. But how should I make it inside?

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:57.200
If it's only me, I could handle it. But I'll have to bring Cream and Cheese with me, so I can't get too reckless.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:04.210
Abnormality detected in the electrical system...

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:07.380
Abnormality detected in the electrical system...

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:13.220
What's up?!

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:14.760
I can't see a thing!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:17.970
What was that?!

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:19.020
What was that sound?!

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:23.860
Sonic...

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:27.440
Cut it out...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.070
Who is it?!

00:15:29.650 --> 00:15:30.490
We're going to run for it.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:31.030
Okay.

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:39.620
A paper plane?

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.840
Absurd! Who did this?

00:15:47.340 --> 00:15:50.010
Never mind that! Get the electricity back working on the double!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:50.590
Right!

00:15:57.640 --> 00:16:00.230
Did you do this too, Mr. Sonic?

00:16:00.350 --> 00:16:02.850
No, I didn't. Just randomly happened.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:08.650
You probably have the power to summon good luck.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:09.900
You think so?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:21.790
Could it be? I'm sorry, because I said something I shouldn't have.

00:16:21.830 --> 00:16:23.210
It has nothing to do with you.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:27.920
Shit! Let's go!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.630
Okay!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:44.060
Sonic. What's the matter?! Are you all right?!

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:46.770
No problem.

00:16:50.190 --> 00:16:50.940
Run!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:51.860
But…

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.170
I said run!

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:12.510
Okay!

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.760
D2 area blocked off.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.310
We're going to be locked in!

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:24.140
Oops!

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:40.580
What are those?!

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.380
What's going on?

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:55.510
I don't know, but now's our chance!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:05.140
There are a multitude of intruders... Multitude of intruders...

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:15.570
The laser surveillance cameras are out of control!

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:29.120
You honestly aren't doing all this, Mr. Sonic?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.500
I told you no!

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:06.910
We're safe now. You were scared. Weren't you, lady?

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:11.040
No. Thank you, Sonic.

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:13.790
Ah, it was nothing really.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:17.380
This sound is...

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:24.970
It's the sound of a plane.

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.140
Oh I see.

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:34.650
I wonder if it's just about here?

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:39.400
Perfect calculation!

00:19:49.910 --> 00:19:50.460
Hi there.

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:52.040
Hi!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.840
I see. So it was you, Tails.

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.050
Hang on tight, so you don't fall off!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:11.100
So shall we get going too then?

00:20:19.940 --> 00:20:24.320
I'm Chris. I just got to be friends with Sonic last night.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:30.370
I'm Tails! I always hang around with Sonic. Right, Sonic?

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:32.250
Sort of.

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:36.750
I'm Cream and this is my friend, Cheese.

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:38.920
Nice to meet you.

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:44.340
Yeah, same here. It seems we'll become good friends.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:46.720
He's my grandfather.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:48.470
Fantastic!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:52.310
I've never seen such micron sized radio controlled planes before.

00:20:53.440 --> 00:20:55.690
Something like this is no big deal.

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.730
But... You're too reckless!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:03.070
You're dealing with the military, you know! War could've broke out.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.410
It'll work out somehow.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.120
That's not the point.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:17.290
No, well, this is really fantastic. Where did you learn all this scientific technology?

00:21:12.290 --> 00:21:15.750
<i>Sonic, are you listening to me?</i>

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:20.750
Where? All I can say is that I learned it in the world that I came from.

00:21:18.170 --> 00:21:20.130
<i>I told you it was dangerous.</i>

00:21:21.550 --> 00:21:24.470
So where is that world?

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:24.470
<i>It was fine this time because everything went well.</i>

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:29.850
<i>Are you listening to me, Sonic? Sonic!</i>

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:29.850
I wonder? We were thrown into this world through a warp in space.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:35.690
Hmm. Very interesting! Very very interesting!

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:37.190
My god!

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:47.030
Uh, Sonic. If you, I, Cream and Cheese were all affected by that accident, could it also be that...

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:52.080
all the others are here too?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:57.790
The others who were there at that time were Knuckles, Amy and...

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.710
Dr. Eggman!

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:25.650
Oh. So we were thrown into this world by Chaos Control, eh?

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:31.990
Oh well. I'll establish the foundation for the Eggman Empire in this world.

00:22:32.240 --> 00:22:35.540
Then I'll expand my territory to other worlds!

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:48.840
